      "role": "EN-READ-F",
      "source": "reading.text",
      "tts_text": "At the reserve gate, a notice described two walking routes. Both paths passed through woodland, but neither reached the lake directly. Either route offered a view from a lookout, although one was shorter. The ranger explained that both footbridges had been checked that morning. None of the marker posts showed the new detour, so visitors needed to follow the blue arrows. A family chose the western path because it stayed close to the visitor centre. Another group took the eastern route and stopped beside the marsh. By late afternoon, both groups had returned safely, and neither had disturbed the nesting birds.",
